      "text": "We have that $|n + 6| = 2 - n$.\n\nThis amounts to the following two cases: $n + 6 = 2 - n$ and $-(n + 6) = 2 - n$.\n\nFor the first case, we have that $2n + 6 = 2$, so $n = -2$.\n\nFor the second case, we have that $-n - 6 = 2 - n$, which simplifies to $-6 = 2$. Therefore, this is not the case, and there is no solution.\n\nConclusion: $n = \\boxed{-2}$.",
